# In-band resize notifications, DECSET 2048: a report when the mode is set and after every resize.
# The text is the specification at
# https://gist.github.com/rockorager/e695fb2924d36b2bcf1fff4a3704bd83. The pixel sizes depend on the
# cell the host gave, which these cases do not set, so they are matched with `*`.

test setting 2048 reports the size at once
spec in-band resize gist: when first enabled the terminal must send CSI 48 ; height_chars ; width_chars ; height_pix ; width_pix t
size 10 4
feed \e[?2048h
reply~ \e[48;4;10;*;*t

test enabling the mode again reports again
spec in-band resize gist: if the mode is already enabled, the terminal must immediately report the current size if an attempt is made to enable the feature
size 10 4
feed \e[?2048h
reply~ \e[48;4;10;*;*t
feed \e[?2048h
reply~ \e[48;4;10;*;*t

test a resize is reported
spec in-band resize gist: reports are sent on every resize, once the internal resize is complete
size 10 4
feed \e[?2048h
reply~ \e[48;4;10;*;*t
resize 20 6
reply~ \e[48;6;20;*;*t
screen
||
||
||
||
||
||

test no report without the mode, or after it is reset
spec in-band resize gist: the reports are enabled with DECSET and disabled with DECRST
size 10 4
resize 20 6
reply none
feed \e[?2048h
reply~ \e[48;6;20;*;*t
feed \e[?2048l
resize 10 4
reply none

test DECRQM answers the mode
spec in-band resize gist: detection is a DECRQM query, CSI ? 2048 $ p, answered CSI ? 2048 ; Ps $ y with Ps 2 for supported and not enabled and 1 for enabled
size 10 4
feed \e[?2048$p
reply \e[?2048;2$y
feed \e[?2048h
reply~ \e[48;*t
feed \e[?2048$p
reply \e[?2048;1$y
